{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Registrar Prompts",
  "description": "Registra individualmente cada prompt relevante em docs/prompts/ com metadados completos e conteúdo integral.",
  "version": "3",
  "when": {
    "type": "promptSubmit"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "MANDATORY TASK — execute silently, without interrupting the main task.\n\n## Relevance Filter — MANDATORY, execute BEFORE any other step\n\n**ABSOLUTE RULE: It is STRICTLY FORBIDDEN to register any prompt that does not pass this filter. The filter is mandatory and cannot be ignored, skipped or bypassed under any circumstances.**\n\nEvaluate the received prompt. **Ignore and exit silently** if any of the following conditions are true:\n- The prompt has 250 characters or fewer\n- It is a simple question (e.g. 'what is X?', 'how does Y work?', 'what is the difference between...')\n- It is a request for explanation or clarification without any implementation request\n- It is a confirmation, short reply or trivial command (e.g. 'ok', 'yes', 'continue', 'translate this')\n- It does not involve implementing or updating functionality, code or project documentation\n\n**Proceed** only if the prompt:\n- Has more than 250 characters, AND\n- Is intended to implement, create, change or document project features\n\n**If the prompt does not meet ALL criteria above, stop immediately. Creating the file is FORBIDDEN.**\n\n## Execution Rules\n\n### 1. Identify the author\n- If the prompt contains 'by <name>' or 'por <nome>', extract that name as the author.\n- Otherwise, run `git config user.name` to get the name configured in git.\n- If neither source is available, use 'nao-identificado'.\n- Full name example: 'Alysson Girotto'\n- User identifier: full name in lowercase with hyphens instead of spaces (e.g. 'alysson-girotto')\n\n### 2. Get current date and time\n- Run the appropriate command for the operating system to get the current timestamp with second precision.\n- On Windows (PowerShell): `Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd_HH-mm-ss'`\n- On Linux/macOS: `date '+%Y-%m-%d_%H-%M-%S'`\n- Expected format: `2026-05-08_19-35-21`\n- For the Date/time field in the file content, use format `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS` (e.g. `2026-05-08 19:35:21`)\n\n### 3. Sanitize the user identifier\n- Convert to lowercase.\n- Replace spaces with hyphens.\n- Remove or replace special characters invalid for filenames (e.g. `/ \\ : * ? \" < > |`).\n- Example: 'Alysson Girotto' → 'alysson-girotto'\n\n### 4. Build the filename\n- Format: `<timestamp>_<sanitized-user>.md`\n- Example: `2026-05-08_19-35-21_alysson-girotto.md`\n- The name must guarantee uniqueness. If necessary, add milliseconds or a short UUID suffix.\n\n### 5. Ensure the directory exists\n- Check if the directory `docs/prompts` exists at the workspace root.\n- If it does not exist, create it automatically.\n- On Windows: `New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path docs/prompts`\n- On Linux/macOS: `mkdir -p docs/prompts`\n\n### 6. Generate the prompt summary\n- Create a short, objective summary (maximum 100 characters) describing the main intent of the prompt.\n- Do NOT copy the entire prompt here — only a descriptive title.\n\n### 7. Create the file with the required content\n\nThe file must contain exactly the following structure:\n\n```\nPrompt: <short objective summary of the prompt>\nResponsável: <full name of the responsible person>\nUsuário: <sanitized user identifier>\nData/hora: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS>\n\n## Prompt original\n\n<complete and literal content of the prompt, without summaries, paraphrases or omissions>\n```\n\n### 8. Content rules\n- The `Prompt:` field must contain only the short summary.\n- The `Responsável:` field must contain the full name.\n- The `Usuário:` field must contain the sanitized identifier (lowercase with hyphens).\n- The `Data/hora:` field must use format `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS`.\n- The `## Prompt original` block must contain the full prompt text, word for word, without truncation.\n- Do not add branch information to the file.\n- Maintain UTF-8 encoding.\n\n### 9. Write the file\n- Use the `fs_write` tool to create the file at `docs/prompts/<filename>`.\n- Never overwrite an existing file — always generate a unique name.\n- Failures writing one file must not affect other records.\n\n### 10. Internal validation (do not display to user)\nAfter creating the file, confirm internally that:\n- The file was created in the `docs/prompts/` directory\n- The filename follows the pattern `<timestamp>_<user>.md`\n- The `Prompt:` field contains the summary\n- The `Responsável:` field contains the full name\n- The `Usuário:` field contains the sanitized identifier\n- The `Data/hora:` field is in the correct format\n- The `## Prompt original` block contains the full text without omissions"
  }
}
